Chapter: CpuPark
  cites Kernel chapter Hpet

 `cpu-park` halts until the next interrupt. Under codex-vm 200 parks took
 439,996 us of HPET time and 200 empty iterations 15 us, measured
 2026-09-23, so a park that did not halt would sit near the spin and a
 factor of 100 separates them with two orders of magnitude to spare. The parked guest
 used 0.28 host CPU-seconds where a spinning one used 4.14 over the same four
 HPET seconds.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  park-n : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  park-n (n) (acc) = if n <= 0 then acc else park-n (n - 1) (acc + cpu-park)

  spin-n : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spin-n (n) (acc) = if n <= 0 then acc else spin-n (n - 1) (acc + 0)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let started = hpet-start
    in let h0 = hpet-ticks
    in let answers = park-n 200 0
    in let h1 = hpet-ticks
    in let spun = spin-n 200 0
    in let h2 = hpet-ticks
    in act
      print-line-uni ("answers " & show answers & " " & show spun)
      print-line-uni ("hpet running: " & (if h2 > h0 then "True" else "False"))
      print-line-uni ("parks outlast spins 100x: " & (if h1 - h0 > 100 * (h2 - h1 + 1) then "True" else "False"))
    end
  end
